sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/development-containers.md#t3-registration-and-pairing): how Orbit registers a container's T3 server with the Conn layer. The step runs inside the Instance-create flow and wake, and in a daily renewal run. The container cannot call the Gateway, so the Gateway records the server from the run's result, with the checks of `POST /conn/environments` (docs/reference/conn.md#registration).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · step of create, wake, renewal
  %% kind: conn.environment_renew
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Conn layer
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant C as Container<br/>via incus exec
  Note over GW: Find sessions to renew<br/>daily · under 7 days left
  %%> When:
  %%> - create and wake run the same steps inside their own runs; this daily check only covers running containers
  %%> Skips:
  %%> - a sleeping Instance: its wake renews the session
  %%> Result:
  %%> - one task per T3 server, with the Instance lock; the intent names a fresh vault key for the session
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-conn-renew
  SW->>C: Issue the Gateway session<br/>t3 auth session issue
  %%> Command, as `agent`:
  %%> - `t3 auth session issue --label "Orbit Gateway" --token-only`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the session goes to the vault key that the intent names, as a sensitive output, never into the run's inputs, outputs or logs
  %%> Why the label:
  %%> - after recording, the Gateway's cleanup revokes earlier `Orbit Gateway` sessions on this server
  SW->>C: Issue the Swamp session<br/>t3 auth session issue
  %%> Command, as `agent`:
  %%> - `t3 auth session issue --label "Orbit Swamp" --token-only`, with only the scopes the thread tools and `orchestration.forceStopThread` need
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the session goes to the Instance's Swamp vault key, which Swamp reads when it drives T3 for a task; it never enters the run or the Gateway's records
  %%> When:
  %%> - never while a task turn operation of the Instance runs, because T3 keeps request ids per session
  %%> Why:
  %%> - Swamp drives T3 for a task with its own session, revoked on its own
  SW->>C: Check the sessions<br/>well-known · auth session
  %%> What it does, the checks of `POST /conn/environments`, inside the container:
  %%> - reads the environment id from `/.well-known/t3/environment`; on a renewal it must equal the recorded one, else `conn.environment_mismatch`
  %%> - T3 must accept both sessions at `/api/auth/session`, else `conn.session_rejected`
  %%> - the Gateway session must carry `access:read` and `access:write`, else `conn.admin_scope_missing`
  %%> Why here:
  %%> - the Gateway records the result and does not check it again
  alt the checks pass
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>environment id · URL
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the environment id, the URL `http://NODE-WG:PORT`, the session's expiry and its vault key
    Note over GW: Record the T3 server
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - moves the session from the vault into its encrypted record and deletes the vault copy, as the pairing result does with its link
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the server's Node is the container's Node; the record names the Instance
    %%> - cleanup of earlier `Orbit Gateway` and `Orbit Swamp` sessions starts
  else a check fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>check's error code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a renewal keeps the old record and session, and the next daily check tries again
    %%> - in a create or wake, the Instance fails with the check's code
  end
